.TH CBMAP_RESET 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cbmap_reset \- clear all elements from the map
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cbstmap.h>

ccol_retval_t cbmap_reset(cbmap cbm);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Removes every key-value pair from the map. The map is empty afterwards,
and the caller can keep using it.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
cbm  BST map to reset
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success on success.
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
O(n). All the nodes are destroyed and their keys and values freed. The
function asserts if cbm is NULL.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cbmap_destroy (3),
.BR cbmap_delete_elem (3)
